text.section:
The Commissioner may cancel the license of any person licensed under this article, upon written notice sent by certified mail to the licensee's last known address appearing in the Commissioner's files, for any of the following reasons:

Filing by the licensee of a false report of the data or information required by this chapter;


Failure, refusal, or neglect of the licensee to file a report required by this chapter;


Failure of the licensee to pay the full amount of the tax due or pay any penalties or interest due as required by this chapter;


Failure of the licensee to keep accurate records of the quantities of motor fuel received, produced, refined, manufactured, compounded, sold, or used in Virginia;


Failure to file a new or additional bond or certificate of deposit upon request of the Commissioner pursuant to § 58.1-2211;


Conviction of the licensee or a principal of the licensee for any act prohibited under this chapter;


Failure, refusal, or neglect of a licensee to comply with any other provision of this chapter or any regulation promulgated pursuant to this chapter; or


A change in the ownership or control of the business.
